<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_43204eb005113090db3476895a76cc14f70698fd23b8582928d6dd3b8f43e10b_n0013/e_0004> <http://digistrucmed.org/surfaceForm> <http://digistrucmed.org/entity/UFH%20infusion> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/semantic-unit/lu_43204eb005113090db3476895a76cc14f70698fd23b8582928d6dd3b8f43e10b_n0013> <http://digistrucmed.org/titleOrContext> "In patients with pulmonary embolism, thrombolytic therapy is recommended only in severe hypotension or shock21 (IC). In women at high risk for thrombo-embolism, it is recommended to convert LMWH to UFH at least 36 h prior to delivery and stop the UFH infusion 4–6 h prior to anticipated delivery. aPTT should be normal before regional anaesthesia22 (IC). In women at low risk for thrombo-embolism on therapeutic LMWH, induction or caesarean section is recommended to be performed 24 h after the last" .
